real EX = 2; real EY = 0.8; draw(ellipse((0,0), EX, EY), dashed); label(" $H$ ", (EX, -EY)); [/asy]

Now the labels of edges  $vw_i$  have sum \[ 	\sum_{i=1}^p \min \left( \deg_G v, \deg_G w_i \right) 	= \sum_{i=1}^p \deg_G w_i 	= \sum_{i=1}^p (\deg_H w_i + 1) =  2m + p. \] For each of the edges contained in  $H$ , the label on that edge has increased by exactly  $1$ , so those edges contribute  $S(H)+m$ . In total, \begin{align*} 	S(G) &= 2m + p + \left( S(H)+m \right) = (m+p) + 2m + S(H)  	&\le \binom k2 + \varepsilon + 2\binom{k-1}{2} + \binom{k-1}{2}(k-2) 	= \binom k2 (k-1) + \varepsilon. \end{align*}  $\blacksquare$</details>

