*A very fast proof:*

Our notations and diagram will be similar to Evan's one. Let  $L$  denote the center of  $\omega$ , which is the midpoint of minor arc  $BC$  ;  $E = \overline{OM} \cap \overline{BC}$ ,  $K = \overline{LE} \cap \Gamma$  and  $E',Q'$  be the reflection of  $A$  in points  $E,Q$ , respectively. 
Since  $\angle AQM = \angle ACB = \angle AOM$ , so points  $A,M,Q,O$  lie on the circle with diameter  $\overline{AO}$ . It follows that  $Q' \in \Gamma$ . 
