[/asy]**<span style="color:#3D85C6">Claim 2.</span>**  $\angle AQC=90^\circ$ *Proof*: Let  $\angle MQB=x$ . From ratio lemma, we have:   $$ \frac{\sin C}{\sin x}=\frac{BQ}{AQ} $$   From LOS in  $\triangle AQC$  and  $\triangle BQC$  we get:   $$ \frac{BQ}{AQ}=\frac{\sin A\cos A\cos(B+\frac{A}{2}-x)}{\sin B\cos B\cos \frac{A}{2}} $$  Therefore,   $$ \sin C\sin B\cos B\cos \frac{A}{2}=\sin A\cos A\cos(B+\frac{A}{2}-x)\sin x $$  Now,  $\cos(B+\frac{A}{2}-x)\sin x$  is increasing hence the equation has at most  $1$  solution so it suffices to check it for  $x=B+\frac{A}{2}$ , this is left as an exercise.  $\square$ **<span style="color:#3D85C6">Claim 3.</span>**  $S\in XY\cap BC$  is the midpoint of  $XY$ .

