Now, by Ceva's theorem
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin\angle AQM}{\sin\angle PQM}&=\frac{\sin\angle GPA}{\sin\angle QPG}\cdot \frac{\sin\angle GAQ}{\sin\angle GAP}
&=\frac{\sin\angle AEB}{\sin\angle CDB}\cdot\frac{\sin\angle DAQ}{\sin\angle DAP}
\end{align*}
similarly
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin\angle MPQ}{\sin\angle MPA}&=\frac{\sin\angle FQP}{\sin\angle FQA}\cdot\frac{\sin\angle FAQ}{\sin\angle FAP}
&=\frac{\sin\angle CBD}{\sin\angle AEB}\cdot\frac{\sin\angle QAB}{\sin\angle DAQ}
\end{align*}
Therefore, by Ceva's theorem 
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin\angle MAQ}{\sin\angle MAP}&=\frac{\sin\angle AQM}{\sin\angle PQM}\cdot\frac{\sin\angle MPQ}{\sin\angle MPA}
&=\frac{\sin\angle CBD\sin\angle QAB}{\sin\angle CDB\sin\angle DAP}
\end{align*}
since  $\angle DAP=2\angle CBD$ ,  $\angle QAB=2\angle CDB$ , therefore  $$ \frac{\sin\angle MAQ}{\sin\angle MAP}=\frac{\sin\angle CBD\sin\angle QAB}{\sin\angle CDB\sin\angle DAP}=\frac{\cos\angle CDB}{\cos\angle CBD} $$  by double angle formula.
Hence by false position, we have  $\angle MAP=90^{\circ}-\angle CDB$  Therefore  $\angle MAC =\angle MAP+\angle CDB=90^{\circ}$

