&=\frac{z(z-19)(z-20)(z+1)}{z(z-20)}.
\end{align*}
We may assume  $z\neq 0$  or  $20$  (since the problem’s looking for something with an imaginary part of  $11$ ), enabling us to cancel off  $z(z-20)$ , to get  $z^2-18z-19$  is pure imaginary. Letting  $z=k+11i$ , where  $k$  is the real part, and plugging in gives
