By the second equation, we get  $y^{54}=x$ , hence,  $\sqrt{x}=y^{27}$ . Substituting this into the first equation, we get  $3\log{y^{28}}=56 \implies 3\cdot28\log{y}=56 \implies \log{y}=\frac{2}{3}$ . The base of the logarithm is  $b$ , so we get  $b^{\frac{2}{3}}=y$ . Since  $y^{54}=x, b^{36}=x$ .  $\log{x}=y$ , so  $\log{b^{36}}=b^{\frac{2}{3}} \implies b^{\frac{2}{3}}=36 \implies \boxed{b=216}$ .

