\begin{align*}
  \frac{a_0+b_0+c_0}{3}&=\frac{(b+c)/2+(c+a)/2+(a+b)/2}{3} 
  &=\frac{a+b+c}{3} 
  &=m_0
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
  \frac{m_1+m_2+m_3}{3}&=\frac{(a+b_0+c_0)/3+(b+c_0+a_0)/3+(c+a_0+b_0)/3}{3} 
  &=\frac{a+b+c}{9}+\frac{2(a_0+b_0+c_0)}{9} 
  &=\frac{m_0}{3} + \frac{2m_0}{3} 
  &=m_0,
\end{align*}
so  $M_0$  is also the centroid of  $\triangle A_0B_0C_0$  and  $\triangle M_1M_2M_3$ . Therefore, we have
