Invert the line  $XY$  around  $A$ . Then the problem becomes to prove that if  $A, X, Y, Z$  are instead cyclic (instead of  $X, Y, Z$  collinear), then
\begin{align*}
AB \cdot AX + AD \cdot AY &= AC \cdot AZ
\end{align*}
Now consider the point  $A'$  on  $(AXYZ)$  such that  $AA'$  is a diameter of this circle. Let  $v = AA'$ ,  $w = AB$ ,  $u = AC$ . Then the conclusion is equivalent to  $v \cdot (w + u) = v \cdot w + v \cdot u$  which is a well-known property of the dot product.

