Here is a solution without calculating the determinant.
If the system has at least two solutions, the homogeneous system
\begin{align}
Yx+Ey+Az+Rw& =0
Rx+Yy+Ez+Aw & = 0\
Ax+Ry+Yz+Ew & = 0
Ex+Ay+Rz+Yw &= 0
\end{align}
has a nonzero solution. From  $(1)-(3)$  and  $(2)-(4)$  we obtain
\begin{align*}
(A-Y)(z-x) &=(E-R)(w-y) 
(A-Y)(w-y) &= (E-R)(x-z).
\end{align*}
Multiplying these equations yields  $((A-Y)^2+(E-R)^2)(w-y)(z-x)=0$ . If  $A=Y$  and  $E=R$ , we get  $YEAR=2020$ , and it is easy to check that this is a solution. Otherwise, we must have  $z=x$  and  $w=y$ . Then the homogeneous system reads
\begin{align*}
(A+Y)x+(E+R)y &= 0 
(E+R)x+(A+Y)y &= 0.
\end{align*}
Since the determinant on the  $LHS$  has to be zero, this implies  $A+Y=E+R$ . Hence  $2100$  is not a solution, and we necessarily have  $Y=2,E=0$  and  $R=A+2$ . It is easy to check that for these years, there are indeed infinitely many solutions to the given system.

