-----**Claim 3.**  $A$ ,  $S$ ,  $D$ ,  $P$ ,  $Z$  are concyclic.

*Proof.* By the spiral similarity at  $Z$ , points  $A$ ,  $S$ ,  $D$ ,  $Z$  are already concyclic. But   $$ \measuredangle APD=\measuredangle RPD=\measuredangle RDB=\measuredangle(\overline{AI},\overline{BC})=\measuredangle(\overline{AS},\overline{DG})=\measuredangle AZD, $$  as desired.  $\blacksquare$ -----**Claim 4.**  $X$ ,  $P$ ,  $Q$ ,  $S$  are collinear.

