An easy Angle Chasing Problem  :blush:  $\color{red}\textbf{Claim:-}$   $\angle PXC = \angle PYC \implies $   $XPYC$  is a parallelogram. $\color{blue}\textbf{Proof:-}$  Join  $AB$  and let  $AB\cap O_1O_2\equiv D$  where  $AB$  is the Radical Axis of  $\omega_1$  and  $\omega_2.$  Now Let  $\boxed{\angle O_1AB = \theta.}$  By Angle Chasing we get,   $$ \angle O_1AB = \angle O_1BA = \angle O_2AC = \angle O_2CA = 2\angle AO_2D = 2\angle DO_2B = 2\angle AYB = 2\angle AXB = 2\angle ACB = 4\angle AO_2B $$   Also we get,   $$ \angle AO_1O_2 = \angle O_2O_1B = \angle APB = \angle XPY = \angle AYC = \angle BXC $$   Also,   $$ \angle O_2AB = \angle O_2BA = 90-2\theta \implies \boxed{\angle PXC = \angle PYC.} $$

